Times built from text with an offset, and from the clock. Every time comes
out in UTC with nine digits after the point, so two spellings of the same
instant become the same document. Text with no offset, a field out of range,
or more than nine fraction digits is refused. Written to JSON or YAML a time
is a string, and that string reads back as a string, never as a time. TOML
spells a date-time, so a time written there reads back as a time. A .strh or
.strt line carries the time as any other leaf.
